**The question (RELAYED, in the coordinator's words).** Who holds a sensitive-field grant (RD-932), before field masking is built? The ruling of 2026-11-11 (C-248) says sensitive fields (filenames, fax numbers, named-user evidence) are masked unless granted; the earlier Roles ruling (C-241, its third recommendation) says today's viewer keeps what it can read; the two collide for today's viewer, so masking cannot be built until it is said who holds the grant. Nothing waited on this: the audit slice was being built and the next permission work is the role source (RD-929), which the question does not block. The options put: (a) Viewer keeps them: today's viewer and the administrator hold the grant; masking applies only to the new roles once they exist; it follows the earlier Roles ruling and nothing a viewer sees today changes. (b) Administrators only: only administrators hold the grant now; today's viewer sees these fields masked; stricter, but it removes reads viewers have today. (c) Decide with the roles: leave it until the six new roles are built and decide per role then; field masking waits. The coordinator's recommendation was (a).
**The ruling, verbatim.** At the live board on 2026-11-15 the product owner chose option a, "Viewer keeps them".
**What it settles.** Today's viewer and the administrator hold the sensitive-field grant; masking applies only to the new roles once they exist; nothing a viewer sees today changes. It follows the earlier Roles ruling that today's viewer keeps what it can read (C-241, third recommendation).
