**Settles / leaves open.** The denial and role-change audit is on main as ruled and the three test pins are on main; nothing was put on a host: the Deploy demo run of each merge read skipped on both jobs and the demo hold (C-224) stands. RD-576 and RD-590 meet their own Done-when at main (RD-576: the cell carries the mode and deleting the guard turns it red; RD-590: the four d-nomatch cells each isolate one variable of the stored name and every label is true) and move per the Per ticket line. Left open, each named and none decided here: (1) RD-932 stays To Do: the sensitive-field grants (row I-120, under the ruling recorded above) and the audit of allowed and granted reads (row I-122, remainder) are owed; (2) <<KEYF1>> holds the router-relative path in the REQUEST_DENIED and STATE_MUTATION rows; (3) the flood shape (Minor 2) is not filed: whether to coalesce anonymous denial rows per address and window, or to drop the second row of a refused write, is open, and the rate limiter's key on a directly reached server is a property of the proxy setting that predates this change; (4) no cell drives a failing role update with a stored user, so a row written before the update would stay green (not filed); (5) RD-826 stays To Do: item 1 (the wording of a link chain that ends at real data) waits on the chain walk of RD-640 round 2 and item 3 (should a store that cannot be read be named in the export manifest) is a question the ticket leaves to be ruled; (6) the review of 201 judged the risk from js/user-controlled-bypass low for its new GET and HEAD condition and found nothing new at head, and hosted CodeQL read <<ALERTS>> at the merge of 202; a new alert would be a new round; (7) a HISTORY entry for each landing and a backlog entry for items (3) and (4) are owed in the code repository, and this pass may not write those files.
Related: RD-932, RD-576, RD-590, RD-826, <<KEYF1>>, RD-929, [[C-248]], [[C-241]], [[C-224]], [[C-190]]. Recorded by the NexusAI records pass of <<WRITE-DATE>>.
```
`<<PER-932>>` = `RD-932 comment <id>; not moved (LATER: the grants and the masking are still owed)` or `RD-932: not written (<reason>)`. `<<LANDED201>>` prints the pull request 201 title, its file list (6 paths), the merge commit subject and body (the Co-Authored-By trailer removed) and the sentence that the merged head equals the reviewed head; `<<LANDED202>>` prints the pull request 202 title, its file list (4 paths), the merge commit subject and body (the trailer removed) and the sentence that the merged head `17b7511d` differs from the reviewed head `8586c094` by main's merge and the counts file only (print `compare 8586c094...17b7511d`: the six paths of pull request 201, which are main's changes, and nothing else; at drafting that is exactly the 6 paths of 201). `<<READ-DATE>>` is `date +%F` at the reads. `<<CHECKS201>>`, `<<BUILD201>>`, `<<CHECKS202>>`, `<<BUILD202>>` and `<<ALERTS>>` are the same fill-ins as in THE ROW. **Check over added lines (program, case-insensitive, underscore-aware names):** no person's name, no card id, no host name or URL, no credential name, no seat id, no B-number, no `Tuesday`, `Wednesday`, `Friday`; ASCII; controls fire on a planted `Tuesday`, `_by_<a ban-list name>_`, `B1588`, `R237` and an `https://` URL; each heading once; the new key appears in C-285 as `created` once (it also appears in the Settles and Related lines by the template: count those as the template's); an entry for a write that is HELD says so in its Per ticket line.

## THE WORK
**Step 0.** `date`; `df -g /Volumes/Datasec_DEV` (STOP under 25 GiB); copy this kit to `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-15_B1588_SEAT-R237_nexusai-records-201-202.md` (`cp -n`, `cmp`, sha256); REFUSE 1 to 3; create `.tools/b1588/` (`_quarantine/ logs/ raw/ texts/ dry/`). STATUS first line `RECORDS B1588: PENDING | JIRA pending`, rewritten after each step.
**Step 1. Helpers** with `--selftest` (a key outside the four and the new one, a second comment on any of the four, a transition on RD-932, on RD-826 or on the new ticket, to Done or to Release Ready, before read-back, a second create, a second create of the same body, a create while its slot is HOLD, a comment while JIRA is HOLD, a move while MOVE lacks the number or while Build of 202 is not success, a PUT, a DELETE, a label write on an existing key, a banned word, a banned SUBSTRING (`gated`, `incomplete`), `_by_<name>_`, a planted `C-284`, an existing marker, a lost key, a changed comment, any `gh` call that is not `-X GET`: each makes them refuse or report). Run the selftests BEFORE the first write and never after.
**Step 2. Facts and PRIOR WORK.** `CLARIFICATIONS.md`: size, sha256, highest `## <n>.` and `**C-<n>.` by `/usr/bin/grep -n -i -E` with controls; `<<S>>` and the C-numbers derived (print the newest C-number and its line with the control `C-283` present); a heading of yours present, or a sha256 other than the BASE slot's with a newer section that is not yours, is a STOP naming what you read. line 2551 holds the words `Accept all seven recommendations` and the RD-929 description holds `today's viewer keeps what it can read` (print both; if either is missing, THE ENTRY's citation of C-241 becomes `NOT CONFIRMED`). Jira: issue count and highest key (`snap_before.json`), each of the four tickets read whole (status, labels, every comment id, newest comment, transitions) against REFUSE 4, the marker searches (all 0), the create's searches with their controls. Code repository, read only: main sha, open pulls (drafter 0), `pulls/201` and `pulls/202` (merged, merge sha, parents, head, file list), their commits, the check-runs and workflow runs of both merge commits, the Build run state of 202, the Build job log line when completed, code scanning on main, the POINTERS table and counts, the key-set intersection. PRIOR WORK: `/usr/bin/grep -c -i -F` for `pull request 201`, `pull request 202`, `0fdc77f0`, `6335717d`, `Viewer keeps them`, `C-284`, `AUDITPATH` over `CLARIFICATIONS.md` and, for the markers and the two pull request phrases, Jira (drafter 0 each; controls: `C-283` and `INSTRERR-199-13NOV`, which must be present); **a READY without a `## PRIOR WORK` section is returned unread.**
**Step 3. Texts by program (dry run):** build every payload (fill-ins by program, texts equal to this kit's with only fill-ins changed: sha256 of each string against the table in THE TEXTS), validate each ADF with your builder, print them, scan (0 problems, controls fire), check no `<<` left, print the table (key, class, length, sha256 prefix, marker, MOVE yes/no, check printed yes/no), the summary length (under 255) and a fake-transport run of the whole write path. JIRA slot HOLD stops here (`RECORDS DRY RUN ONLY: <n> payloads built, nothing posted`).
**Step 4.** 4a the create (slot CREATE), read back. 4b, in this order RD-932, RD-576, RD-590, RD-826: marker search 0; re-read the key, status and newest comment as at Step 2, else HOLD; post the comment (201); read back by id equal (a one-character mutant compares unequal). 4c the Build wait for 202 if it is not completed (BUILD, BLUF 8). 4d the moves, RD-576 then RD-590, only if slot MOVE lists the number and its check printed and Build of 202 is `success`: `GET transitions`, `POST` the id whose target reads `Testing`, read back status `Testing`, comment count unchanged. Re-read the panes before the first write (REFUSE 6). After the last: `snap_after.json` and the diff (new keys exactly the one created; lost none; changed exactly the four; comment +1 each; status changed only where moved).
**Step 5. Records** (slot RECORDS): before-copy `.tools/b1588/raw/CLARIFICATIONS.before-B1588.md` (sha256); append the section and the two entries (an item HELD gets its sentence with the HELD line, never a claim of a write); `head -c <before size> | cmp - <before-copy>` equal; ends with a newline; ASCII; the check over added lines; no other file touched. **C-284 is written even when JIRA is HOLD** (the ruling is a record of a decision already made; its Per ticket line then says not written).
**Step 6. STATUS** sections: Questions, BLUF, Step 0, PRIOR WORK, Facts re-measured, Jira (the create with its summary length; each comment id, equal, move or reason; every marker search; the Build state of 202 at each write), Records, Closing checks, HELD, NOT TESTED, Hand-off items (**Tuesday's: the delivered mark of the field-grant ruling, naming C-284 and its sha8 and the RD-932 comment id as the artefact; HISTORY.md entries for the landings of 201 and 202; the BACKLOG notes for the two review points left open (the flood shape, the missing cell for a failing role update); the front-end work and the fix of the new ticket are later lanes**), Deviations, Corrections.

