**NOT yours:** any code change (every fix is a later lane); the front-end work; RD-929, RD-930, RD-931, RD-640, RD-958, RD-964, RD-965, RD-966, RD-968, RD-985 to RD-989 and every other key outside the row; every earlier record, STATUS and entry; the branch for the next pull request (its counts conflict with main is another kit); HISTORY.md, BACKLOG.md and all of `2_Project_Files/`, the decision store (you read no card and write none), the demo, Azure, the marketplace; any alert action; any pull request or issue comment on GitHub.

## HOLDS
No Jira write outside the closed list; no GitHub write at all; no statement that anything is built, deployed, fixed or proven that a record or a read does not show; no ruling put in the product owner's mouth beyond the words quoted (the field-grant ruling is the chosen option and what the option said, nothing more); no alert read as a landing condition on a pull request head (a ticket moves on main's analysis after the merge); no person's name, B-number, seat id or card id in any Jira or repo text. **OUT OF SCOPE, named:** any code change; anything deployed; any message to a human; chasing a red Build or an alert; the findings left open (the flood shape and the missing cell) as tickets; moving RD-932 or RD-826. A failed post, create, move or comment: stop that item, find the root cause, re-verify; never retry blindly. **PRIOR-WORK CHECK (standing line):** a READY without `## PRIOR WORK` is returned. No message to any human. Jira writes only where this scope says. Never delete. Shell: no `cd`; absolute single-quoted paths; `python3 -I -B`; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; never a run of equals signs as a separator; never name a shell variable `path`; run multi-word loops under `bash` (the shell is zsh).

